{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2930","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2930","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2930\",\"parent_revision\":\"8fa8a493f8af1aa97fcdd703a3683a3d2c3cc1fb\",\"root_revision\":\"2ca2096dd247a0f85506b994afc2b877345a6b8f71f6d0edb2618f6bb1385196\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-17\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`[tool.pytest.ini_options] testpaths` in the root `pyproject.toml` lists `plugins/development-harness/tests`, `tests_sam`, `sam_schema/tests`, and `backlog_core/tests` \u2014 it does not list `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog`. Verified via `uv run pytest --collect-only -q --no-cov -n0`: nothing under `tests_backlog/` is collected by a bare `uv run pytest` invocation. That directory contains 26 test files that therefore never run in CI or in a default local `pytest` run.\\n\\nTwo places in the repo currently assert the opposite and are stale:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/conftest.py:3-5` (docstring) claims testpaths is \\\"`tests`, `tests_sam`, `tests_backlog`, `sam_schema/tests`\\\".\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_network_guard.py:210` hardcodes `[\\\"tests\\\", \\\"tests_sam\\\", \\\"tests_backlog\\\", \\\"sam_schema/tests\\\"]` as \\\"every configured testpath\\\".\\n\\nDiscovered as a side finding while investigating why the pytest suite takes 9+ minutes to run (a separate timing investigation flagged that `tests_backlog/` carries ~1343s of real background-sync-loop teardown cost that would land in every CI run the moment this directory is added to testpaths \u2014 that fixture-scoping bug needs to land first, before this item is actioned, or CI time will regress badly).\\n\\nImpact: 26 test files' pass/fail status is currently unknown to CI and to any automated quality gate. Any regression introduced in the code paths they cover would go undetected.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced during a pytest timing investigation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/ (26 test files) is absent from pytest testpaths and never runs in ci** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e118544e024ff6a9a1dd9305f38b148dbb35c44d7c923e9a739c1c6d59854e8d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTcyAg\"}"}